HGNC complete set, the reference symbol set for gene-symbol harmonisation.

File:      hgnc_complete_set_2026-09-28.txt.gz (gzip -n -9 of the download, unchanged)
Source:    https://storage.googleapis.com/public-download-files/hgnc/tsv/tsv/hgnc_complete_set.txt
           (HGNC "complete set", the current release at the time of download)
Download:  2026-09-28
MD5:       b1e49ff9b0e9e195603b49925daa76ca  (uncompressed hgnc_complete_set.txt)
Contents:  45,111 approved HGNC entries; columns as published by HGNC.

Used by hgnc_table(), hgnc_map_symbols() and harmonise_symbols() in scripts/00_config.R and by
harmonise_genes() in scripts/00_utils.R. Every dataset's genes are mapped onto the approved
symbols of this release: by Ensembl gene ID where the dataset deposits one, otherwise, or when
HGNC does not list the ID, by approved symbol, then by a previous symbol and then by an alias,
each only when it points to exactly one approved symbol. The same symbol mapping is applied to
the Hallmark gene sets, the gene-exclusion lists and the Toro-Dominguez 2014 signature, so that
all of them share one namespace. The 2026-09-28 file is also the source of the HGNC L and S
ribosomal protein groups listed in EXCLUDED_RIBOSOMAL_GENES.
